                    "question": {
                        "en": {
                            "direction": null,
                            "content": "p and q are positive integers and $${p \\over q} + {q \\over p} = 3$$, then $${{{p^2}} \\over {{q^2}}} + {{{q^2}} \\over {{p^2}}}$$ =",
                            "options": [
                                {
                                    "identifier": "A",
                                    "content": "11"
                                },
                                {
                                    "identifier": "B",
                                    "content": "3"
                                },
                                {
                                    "identifier": "C",
                                    "content": "9"
                                },
                                {
                                    "identifier": "D",
                                    "content": "7"
                                }
                            ],
                            "correct_options": [
                                "D"
                            ],
                            "answer": null,
                            "explanation": "Given, $\\frac{p}{q}+\\frac{q}{p}=3$\n<br/><br/>Squaring on both sides, we get\n<br/><br/>$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n&\\frac{p^2}{q^2}+\\frac{q^2}{p^2}+2 \\frac{p}{q} \\frac{q}{p}=9 \\\\\\\\\n\\Rightarrow &\\frac{p^2}{q^2}+\\frac{q^2}{p^2}+2=9 \\\\\\\\\n\\Rightarrow &\\frac{p^2}{q^2}+\\frac{q^2}{p^2}=9-2=7\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"
                        }
                    },
