                    "question": {
                        "en": {
                            "direction": null,
                            "content": "The current population of a city is 11,02,500. If it has been increasing at the rate of 5% per annum, what was its population 2 yeas ago?",
                            "options": [
                                {
                                    "identifier": "A",
                                    "content": "9,92,500"
                                },
                                {
                                    "identifier": "B",
                                    "content": "9,95,006"
                                },
                                {
                                    "identifier": "C",
                                    "content": "12,51,506"
                                },
                                {
                                    "identifier": "D",
                                    "content": "10,00,000"
                                }
                            ],
                            "correct_options": [
                                "D"
                            ],
                            "answer": null,
                            "explanation": "Current population of a city $=1102500$\n<br/><br/>Increasing rate per annum = 5%\n<br/><br/>Let the population of city 2 yrs ago $=x$\n<br/><br/>By compound interest formula, we have\n<br/><br/>$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA &=P\\left(1+\\frac{R}{100}\\right)^n \\\\\\\\\n\\Rightarrow  1102500 &=x\\left(1+\\frac{5}{100}\\right)^2 \\\\\\\\\n\\Rightarrow  1102500 & \\times \\frac{100 \\times 100}{105 \\times 105}=x \\\\\\\\\n\\Rightarrow x &=1000000\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n<br/><br/>$\\therefore$ The population of city 2 yrs ago $=1000000$"
                        }
                    },
